!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/valid/a-kind-indexes-its-members-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §8.1"
  description: """
    A kind's members are a derived index, written in resolved output on the terms of `subtypes`: computed by
    the resolver over the closure, sorted, and never authored. The closure here is this schema alone, so the
    members are its two ids and not `count`, which is built with `integer_type`, nor `any_id` itself, which is
    built with `kind_type`. A kind is a set of names and carries no `disjoint`: that is a sum's fact.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  valid: {
    resolved: """
      !schema {
        stock_id => !uuid_type {}

        customer_id => !uuid_type {}

        count => !integer_type {}

        any_id => !kind_type { of: uuid_type  members: [customer_id stock_id] }
      }
      """
  }
}
